# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, free of state.
#
# .cloop is the one that matters: it holds state.db, config.yaml and hub.env
# for whatever project the image is being built from. Copying it into a layer
# would bake a developer's secret-broker key into a published image.
.cloop/
**/.cloop/
.git/
.github/

# Build outputs — the image builds its own binary; a host-built one is the
# wrong architecture as often as not.
cloop
cloop.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.out

# Deployment artifacts are not inputs to the image...
deploy/
# ...except the executor controller's chart, which deploy/helm compiles into the
# binary so a hub can serve it to `helm install` (Task 20486).
!deploy/helm/helm.go
!deploy/helm/cloop-executor-controller
!deploy/helm/cloop-executor-controller/**
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
*.md
docs/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
